# --- open source / model-agnostic ---

# OpenCode
# - most-starred open-source coding agent (~180K GitHub stars, Jul 2026)
# - written in Go — fast, single binary, no runtime dep
# - MIT license; TUI-based with LSP integration for 20+ languages
# - 75+ LLM providers from one config file; MCP support
# - ships via npm, Homebrew, AUR, Nix
# - note: Anthropic forced removal of Claude Pro/Max subscription login
#   in Jan 2026; still works with a raw Claude API key
# - https://github.com/sst/opencode

# Aider
# - model-agnostic: works with Claude, GPT-4, Gemini, local models (Ollama)
# - git-native: commits as it edits, strong for multi-file changes
# - 100+ model support; repo-map intelligence for large codebases
# - good choice if you want model flexibility or self-hosting
# - pip install aider-chat
# - https://aider.chat

# Goose (Block / Square → Linux Foundation)
# - open-source agent CLI, donated to Linux Foundation 2026
# - primarily Rust + TypeScript; extensible via MCP / plugins
# - 70+ MCP extensions, 15+ AI providers including Ollama
# - https://github.com/block/goose

# OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin)
# - autonomous end-to-end: open issue → investigate → write fix → run tests → open PR
# - more hands-off than most; suited to longer autonomous tasks
# - https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands

# Plandex
# - built for very large multi-step tasks (up to 2M token context)
# - diff-review sandbox before applying changes
# - MIT; ~15K stars
# - ⚠️ effectively maintenance-mode since Oct 2025; Plandex Cloud winding down
# - https://github.com/plandex-ai/plandex

# Cline
# - VS Code extension primarily, but has headless CLI / CI mode
# - free, open source, supports any LLM API
# - https://github.com/cline/cline

# Pi (by Armin Ronacher + Mario Zechner)
# - newer minimal framework; token-efficient design
# - Armin Ronacher = Flask creator; respected provenance
# - watch this space


